00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.912 size:88% position:44%
-I'm so good. It's great
to see you. How are you?

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.148 size:84% position:42%
-I'm doing really well.
And I was happy to hear

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, you know, a lot of peopl
have been using this time

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.221
that we're separated from
a lot of friends and famil

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:21.955 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to do different things,

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've heard that self-help,
self-improvement

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
is one of the ways that you've
been spending your time.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Absolutely. So,
at the beginning of quarantine

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:33.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got really into meditation
actually,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.534 line:92%
and I started meditating more.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.370
It was something that, like,
I had kind of done in the past

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
but not really made
a lifestyle out of it,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.342 line:92%
and now I've started meditating.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I-I kind of came up with
this new philosophy

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.614 line:92%
that, like, I'm never bored.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
I never have to worry
about being bored

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.617 line:92%
because I can always meditat

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.485 size:75% position:38%
no matter where I am
or what I'm doing,

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.054 line:92%
so that's helped me a lot.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then also just,
like, you know,

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.925 line:92%
building better relationship

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
with my friends and family
and even my dogs.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.097 line:92%
Like, getting to walk them

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
is something
that I didn't get to do

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:06.833 line:92%
when I was working so much

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:11.604
so this quarantine has bee
a nice little experience

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
for me to get to know myself
better.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:17.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so glad you've been using
it to such positive effect

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.144 line:92%
I also want to talk about

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
something you used
your time for.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.981 size:84% position:42%
You wrote a song called
"Commander In Chief"

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:25.485
which is basically sort of
a letter to the president.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.186 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How did it come about

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:29.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you wanted
to express yourself that way

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:33.560
-Well, I was in the studio
with a few friends of mine

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were coming up
with concepts,

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.264
and we were just thinking,
we were like, "What are some --"

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was thinking about the music
that's out there right now

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"Why isn't anyone talking abou

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.338 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
what's happening?"

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
in the '60s and '70s,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, when anything politica
would happen,

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.479 line:92%
music was such a key element

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
to help people process it
and get through it.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:58.118
So I was like, "You know,
really need to step up my lyrics

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.687
and make it about somethin
other than just my life."

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:06.626
And so I started making
more music that is less about me

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.762
and more about the broad scope
of what's going on in the world,

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.599 size:75% position:38%
and one of the songs
that we came up with

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:13.800 line:92%
was "Commander In Chief,"

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was inspired
by P!nk's "Dear Mr. President"

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:20.874
you know, when -- back however
many years ago that came out

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wanted to do,
like, a newer version.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really, really coo
that you did that.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I'm wondering,
because of that

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
and because of
the sort of perspective

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:34.721
that you show in that song
were you excited on Saturday

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:35.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Did you get out?

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:39.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you dance in the street,
so to speak?

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.227 line:92%
-So, I was actually in Mexico,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was on a meditation
retreat, actually.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:49.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when I got the news
it was on my way home.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.237 line:92%
And it was the best news.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I cried. I sobbed.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.874
I mean, it was just
an emotional day overall for me,

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.075 line:92%
because I identify as queer,

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so, for me, having somebod
in the Oval Office

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is supportive of that
meant a lot to me,

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it just, you know,
there's --

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.021 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm also a firm believer

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:11.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
